  "body": "Part of #4023. Follow-up of #4407 (review of PR #4383, class B, item 3).\n\n## What happens\n\n`Exit::new(lead_out, retract)` in `crates/pathkernel/src/entry/exit.rs` does not get the material top. It checks the retract on the same path as `Exit::proved` (`check_retract`), but it cannot refuse a retract under the material top. The converter of `camcraft-motion` refuses an exit under its clearance height (`EXIT_UNDER_CLEARANCE`), so no such exit gets to the moves.\n\n#4407 did not change the signature: the callers are in `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/` (`construction.rs`, `exit.rs`, `plan.rs`, `standins.rs`), and #4406 edits that directory at the same time.\n\n## Done means\n\n- `Exit::new` takes the material top and refuses a retract under it with `RAPID_IN_MATERIAL`.\n- The callers in `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/` and `crates/motion/src/kernel_emit/tests.rs` pass the top.\n- A pin: `Exit::new(None, 4.0, 5.0)` is refused with `RAPID_IN_MATERIAL`.\n",
